' F15 -- Privilege-escalation hardening arc.
' Chapter 5. UML state diagram.
' Claim supported: authorisation hardened iteratively over five migrations,
' each closing a vulnerability the previous step created or left open. Each
' migration header documents its own attack -- a primary-source record.
@startuml f15-security-arc
!include _style.iuml

title Privilege-escalation hardening -- five sequential migrations

state "Initial design" as S0 #FFFFFF : role stored on the user profile
state "1 · Role storage separated" as S1 : user_roles table, not profiles\nhas_role() SECURITY DEFINER\nbreaks RLS recursion
state "2 · Client writes forbidden" as S2 : FOR ALL USING(false)\nWITH CHECK(false)
state "3 · Trigger-only assignment" as S3 : on_auth_user_created\ndomain-whitelisted, then\ndeliberately opened
state "4 · Professor reads rescoped" as S4 : union-of-policies leak closed\nvia course_enrollments join
state "5 · Privileged columns frozen" as S5 #DCDCDC : BEFORE UPDATE trigger reverts\ntotal_xp, current_level,\ninstitution_verified

S0 --> S1 : **closes** self-PATCH of\nyour own role column
S1 --> S2 : **closes** "any authenticated user\ncould escalate to professor by\ninserting role=professor"
S2 --> S3 : admin can never be\nself-granted
S3 --> S4 : //introduces// platform-wide\ncross-tenant read
S4 --> S5 : **closes** forgeable verified\nbadge, leaderboard poisoning
S5 --> [*]

note right of S3
  Opening professor self-signup to any
  domain was intentional -- but combined
  with USING (has_role(uid,'professor'))
  it exposed every student's data to
  every self-declared professor.
  Step 4 rescopes learning_events,
  student_progress and achievements to
  the professor's **own** enrolled students.
end note

note bottom
  **One fully reproduced exploit.** As the anon role with zero JWT claims,
  SELECT * FROM friend_ids_of('<victim-uuid>') returned a real friend's UUID,
  and relationship_status(victim, friend) returned 'friends'.

  Root cause was a four-way conjunction:
   (1) SECURITY DEFINER   (2) caller-supplied UUID   (3) no auth.uid() check
   (4) Postgres's implicit GRANT EXECUTE TO PUBLIC, never REVOKEd.

  Reproduced against local Postgres 18. 13 regression tests.
  Migration 20260721000001_s1_rpc_exposure_lockdown.sql:23-30
end note

legend bottom
  Migrations: 20260122202809:5,16 | 20260502000003:16 | 20260601000000:26
  + 20260615000800:31 | 20260621000000:1-24 | 20260620000000:29
endlegend

@enduml
